Its practical functions are:

Groups connectors that can reach the same targets. All connectors in a pool are expected to have access to the same networks and target systems.
Maps IDIRA services to your network. You associate the pool with networks and target identifiers such as FQDNs, CIDR ranges, cloud networks, etc.
Provides high availability. If you have two or more System Connectors in the pool, another connector can perform the task when one isn't available.
Provides load distribution. Multiple connectors in the same pool can reduce waiting time and provide greater capacity for tasks.
Provides target reachability. IDIRA can test whether each System Connector in a pool can actually reach a configured FQDN or CIDR target.
Acts as the bridge between SaaS and private infrastructure. The actual System Connector runs inside your environment and interfaces between IDIRA backend services and your internal servers.
